// The TEST-layer type-check program (#12511), adopting the mechanism #5286 set
// for `packages/spec` and #5449 generalised, and which 31 sibling configs now
// use. `tsconfig.json` beside this file keeps its `**/*.test.ts` exclusion: it
// is the BUILD config, and that exclusion has a reason — ci.yml gates that no
// test file reaches the published artifact. This sibling puts the excluded
// layer back in front of tsc, and `package.json`'s `typecheck` script NAMES it
// (via `check:test-typecheck --project`), because a config no script invokes is
// exactly the phantom this whole mechanism is about.
//
// ⭐ THE EIGHTH AND LAST OF ITS CARD, and the only one that needed a ruling
// before it could take this route at all. `tsconfig.json` used to extend
// NOTHING, and it was the only one of the six such configs that also declared
// no `skipLibCheck` — so two third-party declarations inside `node_modules`
// were type-checked, and the per-package `TEST_DEBT` entry that recorded them
// could not graduate by fixing any code in this repository. The director ruling
// of 2026-09-16 (maintainer verbatim: 「同意」) settled that as a CONFIG-POLICY
// question: the build config takes one `extends` line onto the repo root, the
// way 73 of 79 packages already do, and this file then follows the family
// unchanged. ⛔ No per-package dialect, ⛔ no ratchet keyed on `.pnpm`
// content-hash paths, ⛔ no residual left behind in `TEST_DEBT`.
//
// BEFORE THIS FILE, NO tsc PROGRAM COMPILED A SINGLE TEST FILE HERE, measured
// rather than read off the config. In ONE run on objectstack-ai/objectstack at
// f6c2eb7c865065943a474d1e49833d6184d76e32 with the workspace closure built
// first, same tsc binary (6.0.3) and same worktree,
// `tsc --noEmit --listFiles -p tsconfig.json` — the only config this package's
// `typecheck` named — puts 328 files in the program, 3 of them this package's
// own `src/**`, and **0** of its 6 `src/**/*.test.ts`. So the zero is the
// `exclude` line and not a probe that sees nothing. Positive controls in that
// SAME run, same binary, same worktree, both packages whose tests are already
// in their own programs: `packages/metadata-core`'s test program 9 of 9,
// `packages/rest`'s 194 of 194 — without them every zero above is
// unfalsifiable. Under this file the count is **6 of 6** (1008 files in the
// program, all 9 of this package's own `src/**`).
//
// ⚠️ MODULE SEMANTICS ARE UNTOUCHED HERE, unlike `packages/rest`'s sibling and
// most of the family — and that is this package's own judgement, not an
// omission. `@objectstack/http-conformance` IS `"type": "module"`, so the build
// config's inherited NodeNext already reads these files as ESM; it is also the
// STRICTER of the two readings, since it holds the `.js` import extensions this
// package must ship. Measured rather than assumed: this layer writes **zero**
// `import.meta` and its only relative imports are `./adapter.js` and
// `./node-plugin.js`, both already extension-bearing, and switching to
// `module: esnext` / `moduleResolution: bundler` subtracts **zero** from the 27
// below. `packages/mcp`'s sibling is the precedent for this shape;
// `packages/rest`'s is not.
//
//   - `lib: ["ES2022"]` IS declared, and here it is the one departure that
//     MOVES A NUMBER — the only sibling in the family for which it does, so
//     ⛔ do not read the family's "measured effect: zero" line onto this file.
//     Against the INHERITED value it is still zero: the root config declares
//     `lib: ["ES2020"]` and this program reports the same 27 either way. The
//     movement is against what this package had BEFORE it inherited anything —
//     `target: ES2022` with no `lib` at all, i.e. the `lib.es2022.full` default,
//     which carries DOM. Isolated by a single-option probe: declaring `lib` at
//     all, in either spelling, moves this program from 2 errors to 25. What
//     changes is where `Response.json()` is read from — DOM's `Promise<any>`
//     against @types/node's undici `Promise<unknown>` — and every one of the 25
//     is that one idiom, `await res.json()` bound without a narrowing.
//     ⛔ `DOM` is NOT re-added to shrink this ledger: `vitest.config.ts` runs
//     this package with `environment: 'node'`, so the undici reading is the one
//     that matches the runtime and the DOM one was the fiction. Measured, so
//     the choice is legible rather than asserted: with
//     `lib: ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"]` the same program reports 2.
//   - `rootDir` is INHERITED (`./src`) and needs no widening, which is worth
//     recording because `packages/cli`'s sibling had to widen its own. Every
//     test file here lives under `src` and none reaches outside the package —
//     measured, not reasoned: the program carries **zero** TS6059.
//   - ⛔ STRICTNESS IS UNTOUCHED. `strict`, `noUnusedLocals`,
//     `noUnusedParameters`, `noImplicitReturns`, `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`
//     and `types: ["node"]` are inherited from `tsconfig.json` and through it
//     the root config, and none is re-declared here. ⚠️ A child declaring its
//     own `paths` would REPLACE the parent map rather than merge into it,
//     silently sending a source-resolved specifier back to `dist/`, so this
//     file declares none. Nothing here may loosen a type rule; if a test does
//     not compile, that is the finding.
//
// MEASURED at f6c2eb7c865065943a474d1e49833d6184d76e32 with the dependency
// closure built (an error count taken against an unbuilt closure is not a
// reading — unresolved-import cascades inflate it): this layer reports **27
// errors across 3 of its 6 files**, held per file and per signature in
// `test-typecheck-debt.json` beside this config. ⚠️ THIS IS THE FIRST LEDGER IN
// THE FAMILY THAT IS LARGER THAN THE `TEST_DEBT` ENTRY IT REPLACES, so read the
// terms rather than the totals — `scripts/check-type-check-coverage.mjs` holds
// the full attribution, which has no remainder in either direction:
// recorded 2, raw 2 (TS2307 x1, TS2304 x1, both inside `node_modules` `.d.ts`),
// -2 dissolved by the inherited `skipLibCheck`, +25 exposed by the declared
// `lib` above, +2 exposed by the root config's `noUnusedParameters`
// (TS6133 x2), ledger 27.
//
// Every one of the 27 is PRE-EXISTING in the sense this family means: this
// change edits no test file and repairs none, and each would have been reported
// on `origin/main` had this program always existed. They are ledgered EXACT and
// shrink-only — a file that gains an error is red, one that loses one is red
// until re-recorded, one that reaches zero is red until its entry is deleted, a
// signature that ARRIVES or VANISHES is red even at an unchanged file total,
// and a file NOT listed there may have no errors at all. ⛔ The 27 are NOT
// repaired here: seeding the ledger is the deliverable, and turning an
// onboarding into a cleanup is how it stops landing at all.
//
// ⚠️ 3 of the 6 files carry NO ledger entry, and that is load-bearing rather
// than incidental: any error any one of them ever gains is red on arrival. That
// is the half of this gate that starts working today. This layer also holds
// ZERO `@ts-expect-error` directives (grepped with a positive control — the
// same grep hits 49 files under `packages/spec/src`), so no pin here was
// silently dead; what the gap cost was the other half.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
